# "Our Principal Loss Was in This Place": Action at the Slaughter Pen and at the South End of Houck's Ridge, July 2, 1863 (a Gettysburg National Military Park study of the 1980s)
# A photocopied typescript whose text layer is a damaged OCR (fiefore for before, tf1.e for the, 6usfness for business, and many stray marks); PDF pp. 7, 8 and 9 (printed pp. 3, 4, 5) were looked at as page images.
# Every quote is typed in the cleaned form with each wrong letter or digit given as a {{saved|fixed}} pair; the study gives no footnote for these statements about the land (the park historian's reading of the property records, as the page says 'apparently').
